T*
(Thanks for your message! It's great that you're trying to improve your English. I know it) Tj
T*
(can feel difficult at first, but small steps really make a difference.) Tj
T*
(First of all, I'd recommend studying for twenty minutes every day rather than doing) Tj
T*
(everything at the weekend. You could listen to a short podcast, learn five useful) Tj
T*
(expressions and write a few sentences using them. That way, you'll remember the vocabulary) Tj
T*
(more easily.) Tj
T*
(As for speaking, why don't you join an online conversation group? Another idea is to) Tj
T*
(practise with a friend twice a week. Don't worry too much about making mistakes because) Tj
T*
(they're part of learning.) Tj
T*
(Finally, try setting realistic goals and keeping a record of your progress. It's also worth) Tj
T*
(watching films you enjoy in English, so studying doesn't become boring.) Tj
T*
(Let me know how it goes. I'm sure you'll improve if you keep practising!) Tj
T*
(Best wishes,) Tj
T*
(Alex) Tj
T*
(Hola, Chris:) Tj
T*
(¡Gracias por tu mensaje! Me alegra que estés intentando mejorar tu inglés. Sé que al) Tj
T*
(principio puede parecer difícil, pero los pequeños pasos marcan la diferencia.) Tj
T*
(En primer lugar, te recomendaría estudiar veinte minutos cada día en lugar de hacerlo todo) Tj
T*
(el fin de semana. Podrías escuchar un pódcast corto, aprender cinco expresiones útiles y) Tj
