T*
(Su consultoría despegó de verdad el año pasado.) Tj
T*
(He took two days off to recover.) Tj
T*
(Se tomó dos días libres para recuperarse.) Tj
T*
(3. Rules and common mistakes) Tj
T*
(Take time off means spend a period away from work or study. Notice the time expression) Tj
T*
(between take and off: take two days off - tomarse dos días libres.) Tj
T*
(Context normally makes the meaning clear. With clothing, take off is separable: take off) Tj
T*
(your coat / take your coat off - quitarte el abrigo.) Tj
T*
(Study tip: Read the English sentence aloud first, then check the Spanish meaning.) Tj
T*
